### IPP-1007 Full backup (users + quiz results) tests
### Put the admin password while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back. Run on LOCAL (server/.env), not live.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Admin login -> expect 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 2. Full export (default) -> expect 200, data.backup.scope "full", version 2,
###    with "users" (password starts with "$2", bookmarks as { language, question }) and "quizAttempts" (only completed);
###    every language and question has "createdAt"
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 3. Content only -> expect scope "content" and NO "users" / "quizAttempts"
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export?scope=content
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 4. Dry run with users -> expect users { added: 0, existing: 1, skipped: 2 }, quizAttempts { added: 0, existing: 0, skipped: 2 }
###    errors: "plain passwords are not accepted", "Please enter a valid email", "unknown user", "only completed quizzes"
###    (admin = existing, nothing is changed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/import?dryRun=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "users": [
    { "name": "Admin copy", "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "$2b$10$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuuJ6Vf1Y0nG2kQ8Wm5a1xYk7rB3d9zXcK" },
    { "name": "Plain", "email": "plain-test@example.com", "password": "plain123" },
    { "name": "Bad email", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "$2b$10$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuuJ6Vf1Y0nG2kQ8Wm5a1xYk7rB3d9zXcK" }
  ],
  "quizAttempts": [
    { "user": "nobody-test@example.com", "language": "php", "status": "completed", "createdAt": "2026-10-01T10:00:00Z" },
    { "user": "{{adminEmail}}", "language": "php", "status": "in-progress", "createdAt": "2026-10-01T10:00:00Z" }
  ]
}


### 5. Not logged in -> expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export


### 6. Restore test (by hand, LOCAL only):
###    Admin -> Backup -> Full backup -> Download. Then in server: change MONGO_URI in .env to a new empty database
###    (e.g. .../interview-prep-restore), run:  npm run seed -- --file=data/backups/<downloaded file>.json
###    -> users added, quiz results added; log in with an old user's same password; its bookmarks + dashboard history are there.
###    Admin -> Questions: questions show their OLD dates (not today).
###    Run the same command again -> "0 added, N already there". Put MONGO_URI back.
